## v1.1.3b1 — 2026-11-25

Changes since v1.1.2b1 (beta):

+ Import Kerberos keytabs into a private Secrets directory and bind them to REANA
  account secrets or SSH runner storage, enabling Kerberos after successful upload.
  Credentials are not stored in workflow/impression trees or returned by the API.
+ Manage private SSH workflow ticket caches, periodic refresh and exit cleanup.
+ Download selected EOS stageout files into Yuki or directly onto SSH runners
  using XRootD. Bound REANA credentials can authenticate Yuki download jobs.
  Partial SSH imports remain ineligible for automatic complete-cache reuse.
+ Accept and persist per-submission core budgets for native, SSH and IHEP
  executors, rejecting the option for REANA and preserving workflow deduplication.
+ Execute SSH APD tasks with CVMFS lb-conda, including optional pinned releases,
  without requiring a runner-local APD Conda environment.
+ Configure the HTTP bind host/port and atomically publish the bound port for
  local Celebi endpoint discovery.
+ Separate REANA and native Snakemake dependencies in the Python 3.11 Docker
  image; include Kerberos/XRootD clients and an EOS development Compose overlay.

Upgrade CelebiChrono and Yuki together and restart the HTTP service and workers.
See docs/release-1.1.3b1.md for configuration and limitations. This source release
neither publishes packages nor deploys services.
